speechtext:
I would not agree with that. He had this to say;
They are a little smarter than the C.C.F., because the C.C.F. wear heavy clog boots when they propose something, letting everybody know they are coming.
At that point Hansard records that the hon. member for Cape Breton South (Mr. Gillis) interjected, "honest, honest". Then the hon. member for Macleod went on to say;
But the Liberal party are smarter, because they put on their socialist carpet slippers and creep up on the public. Eventually socialist legislation is put on the statute books, and some time after the people suddenly awaken to the fact that they have been engulfed in a sort of socialistic welfare state, without their knowing it. The Liberals give us socialism by stealth; that is the difference between the parties.
